From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 03] amdgpu_virt.c: no module version on illumos

The SR-IOV VF reports the driver version from THIS_MODULE->version
when built as a module. LinuxKPI's THIS_MODULE is NULL (illumos modules
have no struct module), so illumos reports the existing fallback,
"N/A".

License: a trivial preprocessor guard in an MIT file.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_virt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_virt.c
index 9e8f7d2b8..0c752602e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_virt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_virt.c
@@ -677,7 +677,7 @@ static int amdgpu_virt_write_vf2pf_data(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 	vf2pf_info->header.size = sizeof(struct amd_sriov_msg_vf2pf_info);
 	vf2pf_info->header.version = AMD_SRIOV_MSG_FW_VRAM_VF2PF_VER;
 
-#ifdef MODULE
+#if defined(MODULE) && !defined(__illumos__)	/* THIS_MODULE is NULL on illumos */
 	if (THIS_MODULE->version != NULL)
 		strscpy(vf2pf_info->driver_version, THIS_MODULE->version);
 	else
